-- title:
--   Dense image of the H₁ classifying map at j(q^q)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an integer $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero carrying a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity $\xi$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction modulo $q$ (the subgroup `levelH q M'`) with the kernel of reduction modulo $\ell_g$, and let $K\subset L((\mathsf q))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb Q\to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and with $\ell_g$ and $M'$ units in $A$; let $j\in K$ have $q$-expansion the $j$-series, and $j\neq 0$. Assume: the three variable-change compatibilities for $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-points, for $\Gamma_0$-power kernel polynomials under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`, and for divisibility of `inLineMulPoly`; group laws $\mathcal G$ over $A$ on projective Weierstrass models that are chord–tangent and have the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal T$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases satisfying the section-transport pins; and the existence, for every $A$-algebra and every variable change resp. coefficient map, of graded ring homomorphisms of the projective coordinate rings realising that change, with irrelevant ideal containment. Let $D$ be the level moduli datum of the rigid data `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …`, whose points over an $A$-algebra $T$ are variable-change orbits of tuples consisting of an elliptic Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant, a kernel polynomial $h_p$ at $p^{v_p(M')}$ for each prime $p\mid M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point $(x_P,y_P)$ with $h_{\ell_g}$ dividing the corresponding `inLineMulPoly` value, and a Drinfeld $q$-basis, with $j$-invariant as the $j$-map. Let $P_0=(B_0,\mathrm{univ})$ be any abstract package representing $D$, that is, every $D$-point over any $A$-algebra $T$ is the image of $\mathrm{univ}$ under a unique $A$-algebra map $B_0\to T$, with $B_0$ of finite type over $A$. Then for every $D$-point $x$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has $q$-expansion $j(\mathsf q^{q})$, and for every $k\in K$, there are $a,b\in B_0$ with $\varphi_x(b)\neq 0$ and $k\,\varphi_x(b)=\varphi_x(a)$, where $\varphi_x:B_0\to K$ is the classifying map of $x$.
--
--   This is the density step for the guarded $H_1$-level moduli problem ($\Gamma_0(M')$ together with a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point at a guard prime and a Drinfeld $q$-basis): it says that $K$ is the fraction field of the image of the classifying ring $B_0$ at a cusp-type point with $j$-invariant $j(\mathsf q^{q})$. It feeds the identification of the coordinate ring of the moduli chart with the function field $K$, being used in the determination of the minimal primes of $B_0$, of the kernel of the classifying map, and of its range.
